<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $304.8 mln April 9.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $304.8 mln April 9.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $304.8 million surplus on April 9 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 9</p>
<p>Exports: $193 million</p>
<p>Imports: $173.9 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $434.7 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $149 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $304.8 million</p>
<p>APRIL DOLLAR FLOWS UPDATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.275 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.421 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.806 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.416 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $244 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures are rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
